# Upload filter for `gcloud builds submit` run from the REPO ROOT.
#
# Both deployments/pipeline_idx and deployments/pipeline_sgx build from here.
#
# Without a .gcloudignore, gcloud falls back to .gitignore — which would send
# the 684 MB .venv/ and 71 MB .git/ to Cloud Build on every submit, and would
# not exclude .env at all because .gitignore's entries are not a security list.

.git/
.github/

# Secrets. The jobs read theirs from Secret Manager; nothing here should ever
# reach a build. .env in particular would be baked into the image, and
# scraper_engine.config.conf calls load_dotenv(override=True) — a stray .env in
# the image would silently take precedence over the mounted secrets.
.env
.env.*

.venv/
**/.venv/

# Not needed to build or run either job.
src/scripts/
nltk_data/
*.egg-info/
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.DS_Store

# data/ is deliberately NOT excluded. It is the first-run seed for the GCS state
# tree, and scraper_engine.database.metadata reads companies.json,
# sectors_data.json, subsectors_data.json and unique_tags.json out of it on every
# run. Keep the matching note in /.dockerignore in step with this one.
